# inc-18q6 phase 3: a frozen adjacent goblin is the melee target. (Not a
# babau: its acid touch re-writes the same status line the attack roll
# uses, clobbering the "Attack:" line the oracle reads.)
# Failed escape must leave the same paladin anchored after the attack.
# Reuses tools/keys/entangled-acts.keys' two-tile tanglefoot dance and its
# eight-wait pin: on this seed, the LEFT move that follows those eight waits
# fails its Reflex save (check_entangled_acts.sh hits this same roll), which
# is exactly the anchored subject this check needs.
# No further wait is needed after the attack: on this seed, the very next
# escape attempt already fails both the Escape Artist and Strength checks,
# so the fixture measures a refusal rather than an escape.
@include chargen-paladin.keys
@until "Afoot" ESC
w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN*10
SPACE
ESC
w
K
RIGHT
ENTER
TAB
j
w
K
RIGHT RIGHT
ENTER
TAB
j
RIGHT
@while "Confirm" y
@until " Entangled |" RIGHT
SPACE SPACE
d
ESC
.*8
LEFT
@while "Confirm" y
@dump:anchored
SPACE SPACE
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Goblinkin"
@choose "goblin"
UP
ENTER
@dump:before-attack
UP
@while "[yn]" y
@dump:attacked
SPACE SPACE
LEFT
@while "Confirm" y
@dump:refused
@quit
